<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      The hardened runtime (codesign's runtime option, which notarization
      requires) blocks every TCC-gated device the app does not claim here.

      Microphone: without this key, AVCaptureDevice.requestAccess(for: .audio)
      is denied at once: no system prompt, and the app never appears under
      System Settings > Privacy & Security > Microphone, so there is nothing
      the person can switch on. A `make run` build is not hardened and prompts
      normally, which is how notarized builds shipped through v0.10.0-rc.7
      with voice silently unavailable.

      Screen Recording is TCC-only and needs no entitlement; a camera would
      need com.apple.security.device.camera the same way.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
